sentences.l:
The horsemen first, with horses and chariots,
and the foot-soldiers behind he stationed, many and good,
to be a fence against war;

sentences.t:
ὦ υἱὲ Πετεῶο διοτρεφέος βασιλῆος,
καὶ σὺ κακοῖσι δόλοισι κεκασμένε κερδαλεόφρον
τίπτε καταπτώσσοντες ἀφέστατε, μίμνετε δ’ ἄλλους;

sentences.tr:
ō huie Peteōo diotrepheos basilēos,
kai sy kakoisi doloisi kekasmene kerdaleophron
tipte kataptōssontes aphestate, mimnete d’ allous;

sentences.l:
You will see, if you wish, and if these things concern you,
the dear father of Telemachus, mingled with the front-fighters
of the horse-taming Trojans;
